From 48f0cb6e7ac5b46a6a4e64fef9c059ac322c8e26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelbie <kevin@kelbie.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:30:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): prepare exact sends without contacting the mint

Preparing a send refreshes mint metadata older than five minutes and fails
when the mint is unreachable, although sending stored proofs as they are
creates no outputs and needs nothing from the mint.

Add an `offline` option to `ops.send.prepare`. It selects and reserves from
stored proofs and keysets in one transaction, without a refresh, active
keyset or seed. A request that would need the mint is refused with the new
`OfflineSendError` before anything is reserved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
